        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add plan-first Claw status and remove",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add experimental `claws status [claw-or-agent]` for agent, workspace-file, partial-state, and package-reference visibility\n- add plan-first `claws remove <claw-or-agent> --dry-run --json` with separate `--yes` consent\n- reuse canonical agent deletion and identity-safe managed-file cleanup\n- uninstall a final, unchanged Claw-installed plugin or skill through its existing owner lifecycle\n- retain pre-existing, shared, pending, modified, missing, or ambiguous artifacts and report why\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the status/remove slice for the grouped one-Claw/one-agent contract. Package names resolve an install only when unambiguous; final agent ids always work and disambiguate repeated adds.\n\nRemove revalidates the agent digest, managed files, and package decisions before mutation. Agent drift and unsafe workspace paths block the plan. Missing files are already removed, locally modified files are retained, and unchanged files are moved to nonce staging paths before final digest validation and deletion.\n\nPackage removal is ownership-aware. A completed `claw-installed` skill is removed only from its owning agent workspace after strict ClawHub origin, lock, version, and `SKILL.md` digest validation. A plugin is removed only when no other Claw references its ClawHub package and its installed identity/version still match; execution delegates to the canonical plugin uninstall command. When the original installing Claw is removed while another Claw still references a global plugin, ownership transfers to a surviving reference so the eventual final removal remains correct. Package-plan changes after dry-run fail revalidation instead of escalating consent.\n\nIf package or file cleanup fails after the agent config commit, the root ledger remains partial and subordinate references stay available for status/doctor recovery. All commands remain gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`, and JSON contracts remain experimental.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102228 package installation, ownership, and references\n- This PR: lifecycle visibility and conservative ownership-aware cleanup\n- Next: #102306 portable export from the same provenance ledger\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo`\n- focused Oxlint: 0 warnings, 0 errors\n- 46 focused unit, CLI, plugin, and lifecycle E2E tests\n- `git diff --check`\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n`src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts` invokes the real `src/entry.ts` CLI in an isolated state directory and passes the complete add -> status -> remove dry-run -> consented remove flow. The final result is `openclaw.clawRemoveResult.v1` with `status: \"complete\"`; canonical agent config is removed and the managed workspace file is deleted.\n",
        "branch": "user/giodl/claws-pr6-lifecycle",
